+
+### Scope
+- cross-cutting
+- Protocol map generation, STM rule enablement, and external map-path selection.
+
+### Completed
+- Added enabled and stream_name to the protocol map schema.
+- STM ignores disabled rules before decode-as, FEC, and observation-rule construction.
+- Added the Protocol map page with row add/delete, enabled switch, RTP FEC, VLAN, stream name, observe mode, and Apply action.
+- Added a server API that persists the map and updates configs.protocol_map in an externally configured STM unified config file.
+
+- Updated client-side GET error handling so Protocol map setup failures display the API error detail instead of only HTTP 400.
+### Decisions
+- The configured map path must be relative to the STM unified config directory.
+- Apply never restarts STM; the UI reports restart required.
+
+### Verification
+- cmake --build /tmp/stm-be-build -j2 succeeded.
+- npm run typecheck and npm run build succeeded.
+- Temporary-file verification confirmed path changes, parent-directory creation, and protocol map persistence.
+
+### Remaining
+- Start the frontend server with --stm-config-file pointing to the STM unified config file in each deployment.
+- Verify the page in a browser against a live STM/projector/frontend deployment and restart STM to verify the new mapping.
+
+### Risks and blockers
+- STM does not currently provide a safe UI-triggered restart mechanism.
+
